  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BR2_WORKER_PLACE",
    "dynamic_line": "Maintenance.  Pipes.  Somebody built all this to carry something somewhere, and it never stopped running.  Upstairs they call it Level Two.  We just call it the job.  Corridors go in a grid, more or less.  The middle lines always go through.  The side ones lie."
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BR2_WORKER_HEAT",
    "dynamic_line": "You don't.  You drink, you strip down, you stay out of the boiler rooms unless you need what's in them.  See a red wheel with a BLEED tag?  Turn it.  Shuts the leaks for a couple of days.  Loud, though.  Things hear it."
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BR2_WORKER_DEEPER",
    "dynamic_line": "Ladders go up to the car park, if you find one.  Down?  There's talk.  Hatches past the biggest boilers, offices down there, desks and quiet.  Nobody I know has gone and come back to say.  Don't go looking yet.  Not till you know the tunnels."
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BR2_WORKER_STORY",
    "dynamic_line": "<br2_worker_story>"
  },
  {
    "type": "snippet",
    "category": "<br2_worker_greet>",
    "text": [
      "Shut the door behind you, if you can find it.  Heat gets in.",
      "New face.  You came down the stairs, didn't you?  They do that.  Fall in.",
      "Drink something before you talk.  You look like boiled meat.",
      "Mind the pool, that's tomorrow's water.",
      "You're not crew.  That's fine.  Just don't touch the wheels without asking."
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "snippet",
    "category": "<br2_worker_story>",
    "text": [
      "I was a plumber.  Actually a plumber.  Got called out to a basement leak, followed the pipe behind the boiler, and the pipe kept going.  So did I.",
      "Took the stairs in the car park.  The ones that weren't filled in.  Everyone says don't, and everyone does.",
      "I came up from somewhere.  I don't remember where.  I remember water, a lot of it, and tile.  Then pipes.",
      "Night shift at a hospital.  Went down to check the boiler room.  This is a very big boiler room.",
      "We were six when we came down.  We're three now.  The rest went looking for the way down."
    ]
  }
]
